        "1": {
          "id": "1",
          "name": "index.html",
          "language": "html",
          "contents": "<!DOCTYPE html> \n<html> \n<head>\n   <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"style.css\">\n</head>\n<body>\n  <!-- content on boba tea -->\n  <h1>How to make boba</h1> \n \n  <h3>\n    Do you enjoy delicious boba tea?\n  </h3>\n\n  <h3>\n    Did you know you can make boba at home?\n  </h3>\n \n  <p>\n    Making boba is easy.  I always get the quick style that you can boil in just a few minutes. \n  </p>\n  \n  <h4>Important!!!!!</h4>\n  <p>These instructions are for the quick style boba.  If you get the regular boba, they WILL NOT WORK!</p>\n  \n  <h2>Step 1</h2>\n \n  <p> \n    Boil your water and pour the boba in.  Stir until they float to the top, then let them boil for 2-3 minutes\n  </p> \n\n  <h2>Step 2</h2>\n  \n  <p>\n    Turn off the heat and let it sit in the water for another 2-3 minutes, then drain it and rinse it with cold water\n  </p> \n  \n  <h2>Step 3</h2>\n  \n  <p>Pour brown sugar syrup or just brown sugar on top of your boba and let them sit for a long time so they can get very sweet.</p>\n  \n</body>\n</html>",
          "active": false,
          "folderId": "0"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "2",
          "name": "style.css",
          "language": "css",
          "contents": "/* 2) Change the text decoration for the h4 tag to something else */\n/* 3) Add a text decoration property for the paragraph, h1, h2, or h3 tag */\nh1 {\n  color: green;\n  font-size: 24px;\n}\nh4 {\n  color: red;\n  text-decoration: underline double;\n}\np {\n    font-size: 14px;\n}",
          "folderId": "0",
          "active": true
        }
